    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (81.26) headlining the lineup; he is our premier play due to a high-upside matchup against Dobbins. The combination of an elite dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the leadoff spot (+10%) positions him to exploit the base-stealing potential we covet, making him an anchor for our 5x5 Roto needs. **Yordan Alvarez** (65.52) and **Junior Caminero** (62.27) follow as the next most efficient engines. While **Yordan Alvarez** faces a tougher test in Bryan Woo, his elite xwOBA (0.465) and favorable order placement mitigate the SP skill penalty, while **Junior Caminero** leverages a solid matchup against the lefty Rogers, Tr to maintain high efficiency despite a slight park-related dip.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Caleb Durbin** (48.55). He was the final cut, falling just short of the efficiency baseline required to displace the current middle-infield starters. While his elite sprint speed and ability to exploit slow opposing deliveries remain core components of our roster strategy, his projected production against Bachar did not quite match the reliability of **Pedro Ramirez** or the high-floor profile of our other starters. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Christian Yelich** (39.01). His score is dangerously close to our \"below floor\" threshold, largely due to the severe challenge of facing Skubal. Should his status as the #6 hitter be demoted further upon final lineup confirmation, we may look to pull him to protect our precious game caps.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in the catchers and outfield depth. **Gary Sanchez** (42.06) and **Christian Yelich** (39.01) are both navigating the \"Lineup Pending\" designation and the sting of Skubal\u2019s 2.77 xERA. While **Gary Sanchez** retains value through a positive platoon adjustment, any drop in his projected order would force a reassessment. We are comfortable holding **Chase Meidroth** (39.94) and **Dillon Dingler** (37.74) on the bench, as their sub-40 scores justify preserving caps until more favorable matchups materialize. Strategy remains focused on maximizing the stolen base floor provided by the likes of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** while maintaining high-efficiency counting stats from our core.",
